From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hmz007 <hmz007@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:26:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: dw_mmc: support to disable HS mode for SPL

For rk3399, the highspeed mode doesn't work because of
the signal voltage remains at 1.8V after reboot.

Signed-off-by: hmz007 <hmz007@gmail.com>
[ported to U-Boot 2025.10]
---
 drivers/mmc/rockchip_dw_mmc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/rockchip_dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/rockchip_dw_mmc.c
@@ -149,6 +149,10 @@ static int rockchip_dwmmc_probe(struct u
 	}
 #endif
 	dwmci_setup_cfg(&plat->cfg, host, priv->minmax[1], priv->minmax[0]);
+#if defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD) && CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(OF_REAL)
+	if (dev_read_bool(dev, "u-boot,spl-broken-hs"))
+		plat->cfg.host_caps &= ~MMC_MODE_HS;
+#endif
 	host->mmc = &plat->mmc;
 	host->mmc->priv = &priv->host;
 	host->mmc->dev = dev;
